{"title":"2021 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Generalized_Distance)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Generalized Distance)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Specified_Distance)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Specified Distance)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(d=st)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (d=st)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_(Simple_and_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 (Simple and Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_(by_TheBeautyofMath)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 (by TheBeautyofMath)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Chantal and Jean start hiking from a trailhead toward a fire tower. Jean is wearing a heavy backpack and walks slower. Chantal starts walking at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. Halfway to the tower, the trail becomes really steep, and Chantal slows down to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. After reaching the tower, she immediately turns around and descends the steep part of the trail at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. She meets Jean at the halfway point. What was Jean's average speed, in miles per hour, until they meet?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c9209cfbb0a5a659c9d9095c1162e0c20f548a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~\\frac{12}{13} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~1 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~\\frac{13}{12} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}   ~\\frac{24}{13} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"388\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Generalized_Distance.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Generalized_Distance)\">Solution 1 (Generalized Distance)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Generalized Distance)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808d70ce29110acbfa47228747db2e682cf103ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> miles be the distance from the trailhead to the fire tower, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/4/a442ab65f0eeafb8ea058b5ecaeaec4ec5009ce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> When Chantal meets Jean, the two have traveled for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a9fe24b85132a945c1f2f286ed5334c47cc127.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac d4 + \\frac d2 + \\frac d3 = d\\left(\\frac 14 + \\frac 12 + \\frac 13\\right) =d\\left(\\frac{3}{12} + \\frac{6}{12} + \\frac{4}{12}\\right)=\\frac{13}{12}d\\]\" width=\"459\" height=\"43\" /> hours. At that point, Jean has traveled for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles, so his average speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9d3a57709c19173c2f8811dbc7ab80810d138b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{\\frac{13}{12}d}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~\\frac{12}{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"123\" height=\"49\" /> miles per hour.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Specified_Distance.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Specified_Distance)\">Solution 2 (Specified Distance)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Specified Distance)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i><b>We will follow the same template as shown in Solution 1, except that we will replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0b2e07ea3174747c74e85df32b245d2eb21223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boldsymbol{d}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> with a convenient constant.</b></i>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles be the distance from the trailhead to the fire tower. When Chantal meets Jean, the two have traveled for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a64535fec40239f4279ca8fb392c586b0977eaf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{12}{4} + \\frac{12}{2}+\\frac{12}{3}=3+6+4=13\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"37\" /> hours. At that point, Jean has traveled for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles, so his average speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bcdcc6b08ce26e68ca957364f29112ae868dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~\\frac{12}{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"70\" height=\"49\" /> miles per hour.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28d.3Dst.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(d=st)\">Solution 3 (d=st)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (d=st)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i><b>Shortened Solution</b></i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec51eda216482dc8bc7eabf0b33178793ddd0ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = st$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />, so Jean's speed can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf7c39c7998a889d17bd04e222dd991154df6338.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{d}{t}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"39\" />. We know the time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb608425a3908f6dc185d835225e5c3ae843c91b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{2} + \\frac{d}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"113\" height=\"45\" /> (if the total distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808d70ce29110acbfa47228747db2e682cf103ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />), so Jean's speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/c/efcf676823278bfa635b118f34384f9c63c58572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{(\\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{2} + \\frac{d}{3})} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~\\frac{12}{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"190\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p><p><i><b>Full Solution</b></i>\n</p><p>We know that distance traveled is equal to the speed multiplied with the time. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/1358475dab9c64952d8423776bad0cb55ec0ec37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=st$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e81e768e34655f28c3a44dc07beb44c2d3601b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\frac{d}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"39\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808d70ce29110acbfa47228747db2e682cf103ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> be equal to the distance from the trailhead to the tower. Then, originally, Chantel travels a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distance with at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour. So, Chantel's time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b866676822fae37113caf81ac8f13846faeb53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"39\" />. From the midpoint to the tower, Chantel takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0049275faba66d1146c7cab42dc026f0b71cee89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> hours (since Chantel has speed of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles per hour.) Similarly, the time it takes for Chantel to return to the midpoint is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c18344efdb230584516b9b21175bb5bbac169e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, the total time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb608425a3908f6dc185d835225e5c3ae843c91b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{2} + \\frac{d}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"113\" height=\"45\" />. We can can substitute this time into the original equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/1358475dab9c64952d8423776bad0cb55ec0ec37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=st$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95ffe3a56a372af6b4ace65eeef970ff9f96ac69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = s\\left(\\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{2} + \\frac{d}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"45\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b283160a5023f64ee0cf8b4a9c301d7f0f9efbff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{\\left(\\frac{d}{4} + \\frac{d}{2} + \\frac{d}{3}\\right)} = s \\implies \\frac{1}{\\frac{13}{12}} \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~\\frac{12}{13}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"320\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p><p>~jaspersun\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hRFMsxhXQd0\">https://youtu.be/hRFMsxhXQd0</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_2_.28Simple_and_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_(Simple_and_Quick)\">Video Solution 2 (Simple and Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 (Simple and Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/vwtGZVJ0TbI\">https://youtu.be/vwtGZVJ0TbI</a>\n</p><p>~ Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/LonrTlNRk94\">https://youtu.be/LonrTlNRk94</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_4_.28by_TheBeautyofMath.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4_(by_TheBeautyofMath)\">Video Solution 4 (by TheBeautyofMath)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 4 (by TheBeautyofMath)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cckGBU2x1zg\">https://youtu.be/cckGBU2x1zg</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by The Learning Royal\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AWjOeBFyeb4\">https://youtu.be/AWjOeBFyeb4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a hr